BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Curating the Village: Open Sessions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T200000
UID:blogto-236056@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/04/original_image85c9d33a-1006-4a26-80cb-d50de4c91f
 64.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Curating the Village: Open Sessions is a two-day gathering of 
 artists\, curators\, and cultural workers exploring caregiving as both a l
 ived experience and a working condition. Spanning rest\, performance\, wor
 kshops\, and conversation\, the program brings together perspectives on ca
 ring for children\, parents\, elders\, neighbours\, the dying\, and broade
 r communities.\nDeveloped through an ongoing research-creation initiative\
 , Curating the Village approaches care not only as a subject\, but as a fo
 rce that reshapes how artistic and curatorial work is organized\, timed\, 
 and sustained. Marked by interruption\, exhaustion\, and relational obliga
 tion\, caregiving challenges dominant expectations of productivity\, avail
 ability\, and coherence in cultural labour.\nWhile “care” circulates w
 idely in contemporary arts discourse\, it is still rarely accommodated str
 ucturally within programming or institutional time. Through short offering
 s\, shared food\, and collective discussion\, Open Sessions considers what
  shifts when care is approached not simply as a trending theme\, but as a 
 method—one that foregrounds interdependence\, negotiation\, and the cond
 itions that make work possible.\nProgram Dates / Times / Locations\nFRIDAY
 \, JUNE 26\, 2026\nEvening sessions from 6:15 — 9:00 pm at Theatre Direc
 t (1 Wiltshire Ave Unit 127\, Toronto\, ON M6N 2V7).\nSATURDAY\, JUNE 27\,
  2026\nFull day from 10:00 am — 6:00 pm at Critical Distance Centre for 
 Curators (401 Richmond Street West\, Suite 122).\nPlease note: Saturday pr
 ogramming includes FREE onsite childcare\, a shared meal\, and hybrid part
 icipation options to support caregiver access.\nRegistration information i
 s on the Critical Distance Website: https://criticaldistance.ca/program/cu
 rating-the-village-open-sessions/ zeff
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/curating-the-village-open-sessions-toron
 to/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
