BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Footy T.O.Gether: Uruguay vs Spain Watch Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T220000
UID:blogto-236658@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/16/original_image124d12f4-874c-4965-aff5-6798e98c01
 3b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:FREE TO ATTEND! ⚽\nSaturday night football doesn't get much 
 bigger than this.\n🇺🇾 Uruguay vs 🇪🇸 Spain. The world's number 
 one ranked team against two-time world champions with something to prove. 
 Spain arrive as tournament favourites — European champions\, Rodri back 
 fit\, Lamine Yamal on the wing\, and a squad built to win it all. Uruguay 
 arrive under Bielsa with Araújo\, Valverde and Darwin Núñez forming one
  of the most dangerous attacking cores in South America. This is the match
  that could decide who tops Group H.\nLate kick. Big stakes. Bloor Street 
 on a Friday night.\nToronto26 is bringing Uruguay vs Spain to Bloor Street
  as part of Footy T.O.Gether — our watch party series running all summer
  long across three side-by-side venues. 🏟️🔥\nToronto has one of th
 e most vibrant Latin American and Spanish communities in the country. Frid
 ay night on Bloor Street is going to be electric.\nCrafty Coyote | 511 Blo
 or St W\nMezcalero | 509 Bloor St W\nVictory Cafe | 440 Bloor St W\nExpect
  big match energy\, packed rooms\, good people\, and the kind of atmospher
 e Toronto keeps proving it can deliver. ⚽🍻\nWe've packed out El Clás
 ico and the UCL Final and mobilized thousands of fans across the city. Com
 e see why Toronto football keeps showing up.\nThree side-by-side venues. O
 ne great atmosphere. Get there early\, grab your spot\, and let the atmosp
 here build.\nToronto football is here all summer. 🌟\nWho is Toronto26?\
 nWe run Toronto’s top soccer watch parties\, building hype while helping
  grow the city’s soccer culture. Through our high-energy events\, we bri
 ng fans and communities together around the game.\nToronto26 is also part 
 of the Matchday Social network\, a growing movement that connects supporte
 rs beyond the stadium by creating spaces where football culture can thrive
 .\nBecause the game isn’t only played on the pitch. It lives wherever fa
 ns gather.\nToronto is a soccer city.\nwww.toronto26.com | info@toronto26.
 com | info@matchdaysocial.com | #TorontoIsASoccerCity\n* Independent watch
  party. Not affiliated with or endorsed by any governing football body\, a
 ny national football federation\, or participating teams.
LOCATION:Crafty Coyote
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/footy-together-uruguay-vs-spain-watch-pa
 rty-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
