UID:blogto-236937@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/24/original_image8e799595-046a-473c-adda-fc2904d1b0
 c5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Jazz Chisholm Jr. discusses his go-ahead homer vs. the Tigers\
 , Cody Bellinger\, Carlos Rodón\, and more. Subscribe for daily sports vi
 deos! Stream YES Network on the YES App: onelink.to/yesapp YES' social med
 ia pages: TikTok: tiktok.com/@YESnetwork YouTube: Visit Our Official here 
 <a href="https://www.bonfire.com/miami-and-marlins-find-this-dog-dream-day
 -at/">miami and marlins find this dog dream day at loandepot park shirt</a
 > Eury Pérez Returns From Injured List to Start vs. Rangers\nBy BVM Sport
 sdesk\, 17h ago\nEury Pérez is returning from the 15-day injured list to 
 start Wednesday's game against the Rangers. He strained his right gracilis
  muscle during a game in late May but exceeded the expected recovery timel
 ine. After just one rehab start in Triple-A\, he showcased his arm strengt
 h and health\, prompting the Marlins to reintegrate him into the rotation\
 , which has been reliant on other pitchers during his absence.\nBy the Num
 bers\nPérez had a 4.60 ERA in the season prior to his injury.\nHis last o
 uting before the injury was 6 1/3 innings\, allowing just one run.\nPérez
  threw a 101 mph four-seamer in his recent outing.\nState of Play\nPérez'
 s return brings stability to a rotation impacted by injuries.\nThe Marlins
  had been utilizing bullpen games and substitutes to fill in during his ab
 sence.\nWhat's Next\nPérez's performance in the upcoming game will be cru
 cial for determining his future workload and the overall health of the Mar
 lins' pitching staff as they navigate the second half of the season.\nBott
 om Line\nPérez’s swift return not only boosts the Marlins' rotation but
  also demonstrates the effectiveness of his rehabilitation\, indicating a 
 potential turnaround in his season performance.\nRead more at MLB.com\nThe
  summary of the linked article was generated with the assistance of artifi
 cial intelligence technology from OpenAI\nMLB Miami Marlins Your Des Moine
 s Customers are Here. Where are You?\nJoin our advertising network and con
 nect directly with your local market!\nAlcantara sets Marlins’ career st
 rikeouts record in win over Rangers\nBy BVM Sportsdesk\, 12h ago\nSandy Al
 cantara made history by setting the Miami Marlins' franchise record for st
 rikeouts\, surpassing Ricky Nolasco with a total of 1\,002 during a 6-4 vi
 ctory over the Texas Rangers. He pitched 6.2 innings\, striking out four w
 hile allowing just one run. Alcantara's performance\, bolstered by home ru
 ns from Heriberto Hernández\, Joe Mack\, and Owen Caissie\, improved his 
 record to 8-4\, marking his fifth consecutive win in June\, despite a prev
 ious rough outing against Toronto.\nBy the Numbers\nAlcantara recorded a t
 otal of 1\,002 strikeouts\, a new franchise record.\nThe Marlins built a 6
 -1 lead before the Rangers mounted a late comeback.\nYes\, But\nWhile Alca
 ntara shone with his record-breaking performance\, issues remain evident a
 s he allowed five hits in the first few innings and faced a late-game rall
 y from the Rangers\, highlighting potential vulnerabilities in the Marlins
 ' bullpen and defense.\nState of Play\nMarlins are riding a five-game winn
 ing streak in June.\nJacob deGrom is scheduled to pitch for the Rangers in
  the next game\, adding pressure to the Marlins' pitching staff.\nWhat's N
 ext\nThe Marlins will aim to maintain momentum against the Rangers\, with 
 Eury Pérez set to pitch in the series finale. Anticipation builds around 
 Alcantara's continued performance as he attempts to solidify his record. T
 he outcome could significantly impact both teams as they battle for playof
 f positioning.\nBottom Line\nAlcantara's record-setting game underlines bo
 th individual achievement and team resilience. However\, the Marlins must 
 address their late-game struggles to ensure sustainable success as the sea
 son progresses.
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/marlins-offering-dream-day-at-loandepot-
 park-to-dog-left-out-of-frankfurter-feast-toronto/
