DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T230000
UID:blogto-236284@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/09/original_image7604e159-dd84-4210-9702-a941e43e08
 d9.jpg
DESCRIPTION:MY HOUSE JUNCTION JAZZ FEST 2026: BROWNMAN ELECTRYC TRIO\nAll 
 Fest Tickets: www.eventbrite.com/cc/4844128\n@ My HOUSE\, 2882 Dundas St. 
 West\, Toronto\, 416-604-4555\nJune 22 to 28 -- 7 days of the nation's bes
 t jazz musicians in the Junction's own My HOUSE!\nFrom Press Release:\nTor
 onto's My HOUSE in the Junction live music venue & restaurant has again te
 amed up with Brooklyn\, NY's Browntasauras Records -- who has a studio in 
 the Junction -- to bring you some of the best jazz in the country from Jun
 e 22 to 28. This year again features Artist-In-Residence BROWNMAN ALI as t
 he fest's Artistic Director\, up from Brooklyn\, NY. This 10x Global Music
  Award winner\, 12x JUNO Award nominee & GRAMMY Award long-lister will be 
 on stage every night during the festival as either a sideman or a leader\,
  and has hand-picked all the top-tier musicians & award-winning ensembles 
 involved in the 2nd annual My HOUSE Junction Jazz Fest featuring classic j
 azz\, modern jazz\, latin-jazz\, electric-jazz and more! Come to My HOUSE 
 in the Junction this June 22 to 28 for 7 nights of an unforgettable jazz e
 xperience!\n----\nAll Fest Tickets: www.eventbrite.com/cc/4844128\n----\nF
 EST SCHEDULE AT-A-GLANCE -->\nMon-Jun-22\, 7pm: JORDANA TALSKY: LIVE LOOPI
 NG\nTue-Jun-23\, 7pm: JACOB WUTZKE TRIO\nWed-Jun-24\, 7pm: NICK MACLEAN 4-
 TET play HERBIE HANCOCK\nThr-Jun-25\, 7pm: ARECIBO - Proyecto Blanquito\nF
 ri-Jun-26\, 8pm: BROWNMAN ELECTRYC TRIO\nSat-Jun-27\, 8pm: GENEVIEVE MAREN
 TETTE's FLUX-STATE\nSun-Jun-28\, 4pm: MILES DAVIS: The PRESTIGE YEARS\n---
 -\nAll Fest Tickets: www.eventbrite.com/cc/4844128\n----\nFri-Jun-26\, 8:0
 0pm\, $25 adv / $35 door\nBROWNMAN ELECTRYC TRIO\nElectric-jazz\nhttps://w
 ww.eventbrite.ca/e/1990305160312\nGRAMMY long-listers & 2x National Jazz A
 ward winners BROWNMAN ELECTRYC TRIO is an electric-jazz powerhouse collidi
 ng Black American Music artforms (hip-hop\, funk\, soul\, r’n’b\, jung
 le) with jazz narratives\, extrapolating the ideologies of Miles Davis & R
 andy Brecker. They combine virtuosic performance skills set against an ene
 rgized urban sonic backdrop\, their chart-topping albums “Juggernaut” 
 & the GRAMMY long-listed “Gravitation” have been heralded as "the new 
 standard in jazz" by NPR in NYC.\n:: Brownman Ali - trumpet\n:: Sean Denni
 s - 6-string electric bass\n:: Adam Mansfield - drums\nwww.ElectrycTrio.Br
 ownman.com
