UID:blogto-236424@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_image94e81063-ef4d-4ef2-a76a-8f9ae12129
 40.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Svāhā! On the Land is Nova Dance’s offering of arrival\, r
 everence\, and joy. Rooted in shared breath\, rhythm\, and celebration\, t
 his spectacular free\, outdoor site-specific event culminates in a 30-minu
 te powerful performance and a 25-minute open community dance party.\nChore
 ographed by Nova Bhattacharya\, the work features 9 exceptional dancers tr
 ained in Bharatanatyam\, Odissi\, Western contemporary\, Bollywood\, Latin
 \, Hip Hop\, Jazz\, Ballet\, and Filipino cultural dance joined by 15 next
  generation of movers from Citadel Dance Program and Abhinayakshetra Fine 
 Arts Canada. Their vibrant presence strengthens intergenerational exchange
 \, uplifts community voices\, and deepens the impact of sharing movement.\
 nSet to an electrifying soundscape by Ed Hanley\, Svāhā! On the Land hon
 ours the land and invites audiences into a shared experience that transcen
 ds language and culture.\nOpen Rehearsal on June 26 @ 1:00- 2:00pm\nPerfor
 mance on June 26 @ 6:30pm\nPerformance on June 27 @ 6:30pm\nFree and acces
 sible by foot\, bike\, or public transit. All are welcome.\nThis event is 
 supported by City of Toronto’s Community Celebration Support Fund. Event
  partners: Abhinayakshetra Fine Arts Canada\, Citadel + Compagnie & Jamii.
  Svāhā! On the Land is part of Jamii's "Joy in the Park" event.
LOCATION:David Crombie Park
