DESCRIPTION:Taste of Asia 2026\nDate & Time\nFriday\, June 26\, 2026: 5:00
  PM – 11:00 PM\nSaturday\, June 27\, 2026: 11:00 AM – 11:00 PM\nSunday
 \, June 28\, 2026: 11:00 AM – 5:00 PM\nAbout Taste of Asia\nTaste of Asi
 a is Canada's largest outdoor Asian festival\, held annually in Markham. S
 ince 2003\, the festival has brought together diverse communities through 
 food\, culture\, entertainment\, and family-friendly activities. The three
 -day event celebrates Canada's multicultural spirit with authentic Asian c
 uisine\, cultural showcases\, live performances\, community exhibits\, and
  interactive experiences for visitors of all ages.\nFestival Highlights\nO
 ver 100 food vendors and exhibitors\nMulticultural stage performances and 
 cultural showcases\nTraditional lion dances and martial arts demonstration
 s\nLive music\, dance performances\, and talent competitions\nFamily-frien
 dly activities and community engagement\nFree admission for all visitors\n
 Past Years\nOver 20 years of celebrating Asian culture and heritage in Can
 ada\nAttendance exceeding 180\,000 visitors annually\nFeatured renowned pe
 rformers\, celebrities\, dignitaries\, and community leaders from across C
 anada and Asia\nFeatured Performer\nThis year\, Taste of Asia is proud to 
 feature acclaimed Hong Kong actor Philip Keung. Known for his outstanding 
 work in television dramas and films\, Philip Keung will make a special app
 earance and perform on Saturday evening\, June 27\, as part of the festiva
 l's headline entertainment lineup. His appearance is expected to be one of
  the highlights of the weekend\, drawing fans from across the Greater Toro
 nto Area and beyond.
LOCATION:Streets of Kennedy and Steeles
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/taste-of-asia-toronto-3/
