 gto.com/events/2026/06/02/original_imagedf80f55a-0190-48f1-bd22-f42ca01186
 c5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:One game. One chance for freedom.\nJoin the ICFF for the scree
 ning of Victory\, a sports drama that brings together the intensity of war
 time resistance and the power of soccer. Before the film\, guests can enjo
 y soccer-themed activations and interactive experiences.\nSet during World
  War II\, Victory follows a group of Allied prisoners of war who are recru
 ited to play a highly publicized football match against a German team in o
 ccupied Paris. As they prepare for the game\, the players secretly plan an
  escape\, forcing them to choose between freedom and finishing the match t
 hat has become a symbol of pride and resistance. Featuring legendary socce
 r stars alongside a stellar cast\, Victory delivers a thrilling story of t
 eamwork\, determination\, and the enduring human spirit.\nExperience a cin
 ematic celebration of sport\, resilience\, and the moments that bring peop
 le together both on and off the field.
LOCATION:The Distillery Historic District (Outdoor Theatre: Spirit Cinema)
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/victory-presented-by-the-icff-festival-a
 t-the-distillery-district-toronto/
