 a0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:‘100% Canadian Beef’ is a Pre-Canada Day stand-up comedy s
 howcase featuring five of Toronto’s best\, most polite\, yet hilariously
  petty comedians because that’s the true Canadian way.\nAll-Star lineup 
 showcasing the many faces of what it truly means to be Canadian delivering
  the kind of high-quality comedy that fits in perfectly with the legendary
  Second City Theatre’s vibe.\nThese performers have been seen on televis
 ion CBC\, Crave\, Just For Laughs\, and all over your For You page.\n—\n
 STARRING:\nPatrick Haye has performed nationwide in Comedy clubs and corpo
 rate events. He’s done all the major festivals\, including Just For Laug
 hs. He’s been televised on CBC\; you can hear him on satellite radio. He
 ’s also performed for the Canadian Air Force in Spain. With his storytel
 ling and observational style\, he’s always a favourite.\nAdrienne Fish h
 as recorded four performances for national television\, including an appea
 rance at Montreal’s Just For Laughs Festival as part of Canada’s Homeg
 rown Comics\, airing on CTV Comedy Channel and CraveTV. She has appeared o
 n Season 2 of CTV’s Roast Battle Canada and is regularly featured across
  North America on Sirius XM radio.\nJacob Balshin also been featured on CB
 C’s New Wave of Comedy\, where he has amassed millions of views online. 
 Jacob regularly hosts a Hidden Gems showcase in Toronto highlighting the m
 ost underappreciated comics in the city. The rising content creator and st
 andup puts on a show that few will forget and leaves them with a lasting i
 mpression.\nAnjelica Scannura is a 2025 Just For Laughs New Face of Stand-
 Up\, and the first Canadian woman to win the Boston Comedy Festival. She r
 ecently also won the Jersey City Comedy Festival\, and has performed on ic
 onic stages including Massey Hall and The Wilbur. Her debut comedy EP with
  JFL Originals can be heard on SiriusXM\, and she’s also recorded for th
 e Winnipeg Comedy Festival and CBC’s Laugh Out Loud multiple times.\nDan
 iel Woodrow‘s Stand Up can be seen on CBC’s ‘New Wave Of StandUp’.
  He was featured on 5 episodes of Craves ‘Roast Battle Canada’ of wher
 e he earned himself a Canadian Screen Award nomination. Woodrow has perfor
 med on Just For Laughs\, JFL Toronto\, and the JFL Vancouver festivals\, h
 is calls-it-as-he-sees-it attitude\, and dry\, slice of life humour will k
 eep you entertained and make you feel like his best friend.
