BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Arts in the Parks: The Power of Movement
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T140000
UID:blogto-236830@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/22/original_image43f95a73-c180-4ca5-8c52-e347772747
 da.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This three-week cultural dance series is designed to enhance m
 ental health and overall well-being through African and Caribbean dance st
 yles. Each session will begin with a 45-minute DJ set to create an energet
 ic and welcoming atmosphere\, during which ICONS group members will guide 
 participants through interactive movement activities. This will be followe
 d by a 45-minute dance workshop led by a resident artist.\nAll dance level
 s are welcome\, and the program is designed to foster a safe\, inclusive\,
  and joyful environment where participants can learn\, move\, and connect.
  The series is free\, family-friendly\, and open to the entire community.\
 nSessions will take place at Bell Manor Park from 12:00 PM to 2:00 PM on S
 aturdays: June 27\, 2026\; July 25\, 2026\; and August 22\, 2026.\nRain da
