 gto.com/events/2026/05/27/original_image350f2fd4-4e29-4f4c-8ff2-cb0bf760be
 c7.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Sat\, June 27\, 2-5pm\, Mill St. Wellesley Stage (across from 
 Wellesley TTC station)\nIt’s been 15 years since the first brOWN//out & 
 We Won’t Stop! As the “south asian”* community stage\, brOWN//out ce
 lebrates the magnificent multiplicity of our communities\, and is a space 
 for singers\, dancers\, drag and burlesque artists\, DJs and more. With a 
 mix of first time and established artists\, we’ve been honoured to prese
 nt artists like Sushmita\, Vivek Shraya\, Zaiba Baig\, ROSINA\, D!XON\, BO
 IBND\, Optimal Tease\, and many more.\n*the term “south asian” is used
  strategically: there is no way to adequately represent all the complexiti
 es of identities connected to “South Asia\,” which can include diaspor
 ic\, Nepali\, Tamil\, Indo-Caribbean\, brown\, Fijian\, Maldivian\, mixed-
 race\, Pakistani\, and more.\nVisit www.brownout.ca / @brownoutstage on IG
  to learn more.
LOCATION:Mill St. Wellesley Stage (across from Wellesley TTC station)
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/brownout-2026-south-asian-stage-at-pride
 -toronto-toronto/
