 inocut image to print onto a sketchbook cover and fine art paper. Our inst
 ructor will guide attendees step-by-step through each stage of the process
 . By the end of the workshop\, you’ll leave with a unique sketchbook\, f
 ine art prints and the knowledge of how to set up a printmaking space at h
 ome. Beginners welcome.\nYou can create anything you wish\; please bring y
 our own photos\, sketches and drawings for reference. We will be carving a
  4 x 6 inch lino block\, so your design needs to fit those dimensions.\nPr
 intmaking materials will be provided. We’ll also have Posca paint marker
 s available for adding an extra punch of colour.\nMaking art can be messy\
 , please dress for mess.\nMaterials:\n✸ 4x6 soft lino block\n✸ Kraft c
 over (5.5x8.25)\, lay flat\, 100gsm notebook\n✸ Akua ink\n✸ Brayers\n
 ✸ Strathmore toned paper\nWho is this for?\nJournalers\, artists and beg
 inners looking for a lowkey workshop\, with a finished product to keep all
