 🇵🇹 Portugal. Two of the most exciting squads in world football meeti
 ng in a match that could decide who tops Group K. Portugal arrive with Bru
 no Fernandes\, Bernardo Silva\, and Cristiano Ronaldo — in what could be
  his final tournament appearance. Colombia arrive with Luis Díaz\, James 
 Rodríguez\, and the kind of attacking flair that makes them one of the to
 urnament's genuine dark horses.\nAnd here's what makes it even more extrao
 rdinary — these two nations have never met in a competitive fixture. Eve
 r. Whatever happens on June 27 is football history from the first whistle.
 \nToronto26 is bringing Colombia vs Portugal to Bloor Street as part of Fo
 oty T.O.Gether — our watch party series running all summer long across t
 wo side-by-side venues. 🏟️🔥\nToronto has one of the largest Colomb
 ian and Portuguese communities in the country. Saturday night on Bloor Str
 eet is going to be something special.\nCrafty Coyote | 511 Bloor St W\nVic
 tory Cafe | 440 Bloor St W\nExpect big match energy\, packed rooms\, good 
 people\, and the kind of atmosphere Toronto keeps proving it can deliver. 
 ⚽🍻\nWe've packed out El Clásico and the UCL Final and mobilized thou
 sands of fans across the city. Come see why Toronto football keeps showing
  up.\nTwo side-by-side venues. One great atmosphere. Get there early\, gra
 b your spot\, and let the atmosphere build.\nToronto football is here all 
 summer. 🌟\nWho is Toronto26?\nWe run Toronto’s top soccer watch parti
 es\, building hype while helping grow the city’s soccer culture. Through
  our high-energy events\, we bring fans and communities together around th
 e game.\nToronto26 is also part of the Matchday Social network\, a growing
  movement that connects supporters beyond the stadium by creating spaces w
 here football culture can thrive.\nBecause the game isn’t only played on
  the pitch. It lives wherever fans gather.\nToronto is a soccer city.\nwww
 .toronto26.com | info@toronto26.com | info@matchdaysocial.com | #TorontoIs
 ASoccerCity\n* Independent watch party. Not affiliated with or endorsed by
  any governing football body\, any national football federation\, or parti
 cipating teams.
