DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T163000
UID:blogto-236374@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/10/original_image53937df1-025e-4dda-b11a-01ec7a755d
 21.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Alternity Hub and the Kirtan Culture Initiative are excited to
  invite you for a special event at Alternity (333 Bloor St West) in downto
 wn Toronto. The event will feature an interactive presentation of musical 
 mantra meditation (kirtan).\nKirtan is a call-and-response form of meditat
 ion\, utilizing ancient eastern mantras\, traditional instruments and our 
 very own voices. The event will present an opportunity to explore our sacr
 ed heart space through the power of music and mantras. The practice of kir
 tan can tap into deep states of consciousness but can also invoke exciting
  feelings of joy and energy.\nPresenting this special workshop will be mem
 bers of the Kirtan Culture Initiative who have been sharing kirtan in vari
 ous capacities throughout Toronto for the last 15 years. We warmly invite 
 you to join us for this special event!
LOCATION:Alternity
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/kirtan-music-mantras-at-alternity-toront
 o-5/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Klezmer Jam & Yiddish Dance! - June 27
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T163000
UID:blogto-236526@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/14/original_image091d9d0e-2ede-4410-8383-a5f73bf7dc
 96.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Rad Yiddish and Marching Disorder Present:\nKLEZMER JAM & YIDD
 ISH DANCE with Martin van de Ven & freygl gertsovski!\n📅 Saturday\, Jun
 e 27 @ 2:00-4:30PM\n📍HIGH PARK NATURE CENTRE - Side Porch --- 375 Colbo
 rne Lodge Dr\, Toronto\, ON M6P 3K7\n2:00PM - Set up your instruments\n2:3
 0PM - Learn a new klezmer tune from Martin\n2:45-4:30PM - Jamming & Dancin
 g\n🎻 MUSICIANS:\nGrab your instrument and join us at Taco\, Taco for Ra
 d Yiddish & Marching Disorder's inaugural Klezmer Jam & Yiddish Dance!\n--
 We'll start with Martin teaching a tune\, then play through the rest of th
 e tunes on the set list for the rest of the jam (with a midway break)\, st
 arting with easier tunes\n--Every month we'll share the charts ahead of ti
 me.\n--We'll play through all or some of these tunes\, and change up the o
 rder depending on jam attendee request\n--Some printed copies of the chart
 s will be available at the jam\; bring your own stand if you want to look 
 at sheet music.\n💃 DANCERS / AUDIENCE:\nNot a musician? freygl gertsovs
 ki will lead Yiddish dance. NO experience necessary!\n--Come learn the dan
 ce steps that go with klezmer music! Yiddish dance is a social folk dance 
 danced in circles\, squares\, and lines.\n--freygl will lead us in various
  dances such as freylekhs\, zhoks\, bulgars\, and turkishers.\n--Yiddish d
 ance can be modified for those using mobility devices or need to dance sea
 ted\, by learning the arm movements.\nACCESS\n--There are accessible paved
  sidewalks from Bloor into the location entrance along Colborne Lodge Dr. 
 that are flat and have ramps onto the sidewalk from the street.\n--High Pa
 rk Nature Centre’s Cottage and Forest School buildings are not yet AODA-
 compliant facilities. High Park staff attempt their best to accommodate ac
 cessibility needs on a case-by-case basis. Please reach out to us about an
 y accessibility-related questions you might have.\n--The location has a fr
 ont door ramp\, not to code with a door that opens out and no push button\
 nPlease let us know in your registration if you have any access needs you'
 d like us to address.\nBATHROOMS\n--Closest accessible washrooms are on We
 st Rd near the north gate entrance\, including accessible stalls that are 
 gendered.\nDIRECTIONS\nVIA WALKING\n--The shortest and most convenient way
  is walk in to High Park is from the High Park North Gates. Just walk a fe
 w steps south along Colborne Lodge Drive and the Nature Centre will be on 
 your left.\n---Want to avoid getting lost? Stick to paved sidewalks and pa
 ved paths\, especially if it’s your first time visiting High Park or the
  Nature Centre’s facilities.\nVIA TTC BUS/SUBWAY\n--Nearest TTC station 
 is High Park Station (wheelchair accessible)\n--It is conveniently just a 
 5-minute walk from the Forest School.\n--Listed here are some of the bus l
 ines to help you get to the High Park TTC Station.\n30 High Park North\n14
 9 Etobicoke-Bloor\n189 Stockyards\n203 High Park (summer seasonal bus thro
 ugh High Park)\n300 Bloor-Danforth Night Bus\nVIA CAR\n--High Park is curr
 ently closed to motorized vehicles on weekends\, holidays and during the c
 herry blossom season.\n--Closest paid parking to entrance - 1830 Bloor Str
 eet Parking- Precise ParkLink\nWORKSHOP LEADER BIOS\nA mainstay of the Can
 adian klezmer scene\, Martin van de Ven (he/him) performs with Canada’s 
 hottest klezmer band\, Beyond the Pale. A unique stylist\, he brings fire\
 , elegance\, and humour to his performances with the award-winning group. 
 He has composed\, arranged\, and directed performances for Toronto product
 ion companies including Jumblies Theatre\, Theatre Columbus\, Queen of Pud
 ding Theatre\, and the Ashkenaz Foundation.\nOver the past decade\, he has
  written a number of choral works in collaboration with Jumblies Theatre d
 irector Ruth Howard. He has also collaborated as composer and arranger wit
 h Beth Anne Cole on her recent album\, Perhaps the Gods of Love. Martin re
 cently retired from his work as a music teacher with the Toronto District 
 School Board and is now an active freelance musician.\nfreygl gertsovski 
 פֿרעיגל גערצאָװסקי (fae/faer/faers | פֿײ/פֿער/פֿ
 ײער) is the founder and director of Rad Yiddish. As a cultural organize
 r and multi-disciplinary writer\, fae focuses on heritage reclamation and 
 cultural production at the intersections of queerness\, disability\, post-
 Soviet identity\, and Yiddishkayt.\nfreygl has been participating in Yiddi
 sh dance at Yiddish programs and cultural festivals since 2018 and lay-lea
 ds Yiddish dancing for faer community. fae is passionate about fostering o
 pportunities for cultural belonging and participation through accessible a
 nd inclusive events\, including Yiddish dancing for all abilities and ages
 .
LOCATION:HIGH PARK NATURE CENTRE - Side Porch
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/klezmer-jam-yiddish-dance-june-27-toront
 o/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Laugh It Off: Comedy Therapy with a Real Therapist
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T203000
UID:blogto-236824@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/22/original_image8887513b-e1bd-49ec-947b-5145fdb0ba
 0b.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Bring the thing that's been living rent-free in your head. We'
 ll help you laugh it off\, for good.\nLaugh It Off is the group-therapy co
 medy show. You anonymously submit a real struggle\, grievance\, or thing y
 ou've never said out loud. Then stand-up comedian Andrew Packer and a rota
 ting lineup of nationally touring comedians turn it into the funniest part
  of your week. While Andrew's actual dad\, a licensed therapist of 35+ yea
 rs\, sits right there on stage and tells you what's really going on undern
 eath the laughs.\nIt's part stand-up\, part therapy\, and honestly unlike 
 anything else you'll see live. One minute you're crying laughing at a stra
 nger's disaster. The next you realize it's kind of your disaster too.\nWha
 t you're walking into:\nA real therapist and comedians on one stage\, work
 ing through your stuff in real time\nFully anonymous submissions: share as
  much or as little as you want\, nobody knows it's yours\nStand-up\, genui
 ne catharsis\, and a unique night out that's actually hilarious and weirdl
 y good for you\n"I can't believe how people opened up. I laughed and I fee
 l like I can overcome the problems that were weighing me down."  And our p
 ersonal favourite\, "We need to protect Therapist Jeff at all costs."\nAnd
 rew's a Kill Tony alum with a Dry Bar Special and JFL credits. His dad jus
 t has the credentials.\nOur past two shows sold out in advance. We only do
  this once a month\, and there's truly no other show like it\, so grab you
 r seat now.\n\n$25 online\, $30 at the door
LOCATION:Comedy Bar
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/laugh-it-off-comedy-therapy-with-a-real-
 therapist-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Low Sky\, Lo-Fi: An Evening of Origins
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T214500
UID:blogto-236860@blogto.com
DESCRIPTION:For the past twenty years\, Peter Kuplowsky has championed gen
 re and underground cinema as both a curator and independent producer. In 2
 026\, he founded Low Sky Productions\, a Toronto-based\, filmmaker-driven 
 development company dedicated to discovering\, fostering and advancing ori
 ginal film projects into relationships with seasoned production companies.
  In tandem with its development stream\, Low Sky is also committed to cham
 pioning gonzo media\, be they episodic\, feature\, narrative or non-fictio
 n\, through year-round film screenings and festivals.\nTo mark the unveili
 ng of its inaugural slate of productions\, from June 26th to June 28th\, L
 ow Sky will be hosting a micro-festival of screenings across key venues in
  Toronto that defined Peter Kuplowsky’s career as a film curator\, and s
 howcasing films that inspired his career as a producer.\n"This collection 
 of films showcase the early works of artists that LOW SKY PRODUCTIONS has 
 either supported or is committed to supporting in the future. I curated ma
 ny of these short films during my time as a short film curator for Toronto
  After Dark and Fantastic Fest\, and all sparked friendships that have evo
 lved into professional collaborations.” - Peter Kuplowsky\nThe programme
  features early works from Avalon Fast\, Chris Nash\, Mickey Reece\, Steve
 n Kostanski\, Tipper Newton and more to be announced!\nRead more about Low
  Sky Weekend Here: https://lowsky.eventive.org/welcome
LOCATION:CineCycle (CFMDC)
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/low-sky-lo-fi-an-evening-of-origins-toro
 nto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
