BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TSA Walking Tour: East Bayfront
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260627T113000
UID:blogto-236406@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_imagebbef177e-b344-4c9c-afb6-4baa5d2a2d
 29.jpg
DESCRIPTION:For years\, Toronto’s Queen Elizabeth Docks were remnants of
  Toronto’s industrial past\, covered in parking lots and former warehous
 e buildings that once served the marine-transport industry. Now\, after de
 cades of planning\, an exciting transformation is underway and a new mixed
 -used neighbourhood is starting to emerge right at the water’s edge.\nJo
 in us on a tour as we explore East Bayfront\, a new neighbourhood currentl
 y under construction where design and innovation are leading the way! At t
 he centre of this tour are some of the city’s most forward-looking build
 ings and spaces: from parks and sculptures that double up as stormwater tr
 eatment plants to a new generation of tall buildings made entirely out of 
 wood. Along the way we’ll discuss the difficult task of masterplanning a
  neighbourhood\, how the early guidelines are now taking shape in the buil
 t environment\, and the different strategies being employed to ensure East
  Bayfront’s success in our ever-changing city. If you’re looking to un
 derstand the future of city-building in Toronto\, this is a tour you can
 ’t miss!\nMeeting Place: 1 Lower Jarvis St\, Toronto\, ON\, M5E 3Y5\nFin
 ish: Aqualuna\, 155 Merchants' Wharf\, Toronto\, ON\, M5A 0Y4\nCost: $15 G
 eneral Admission\, FREE for TSA Members\nHost: Toronto Society of Architec
 ts
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/tsa-walking-tour-east-bayfront-toronto-3
 /
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
