BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baracoa - Presented by the ICFF Festival at the Distillery Distric
 t
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T220000
UID:blogto-236290@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/09/original_image1313835d-e97d-4197-ba67-8ef1ed416e
 03.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Three lives. One journey. And a legacy that refuses to stay bu
 ried.\nJoin ICFF for a special screening of Baracoa\, a moving drama that 
 explores love\, loss\, and the search for connection across generations an
 d cultures.\nFelipe\, an aging Italian revolutionary living in Havana\, sp
 ends his final days reflecting on a Cuba that has drifted far from the ide
 als he once fought to build. Meanwhile\, his son Pepe dreams of leaving th
 e island behind and starting a new life in Canada\, far from his father's 
 world. When Felipe passes away\, Pepe is stunned to discover that his fath
 er has entrusted both his ashes and a share of the family estate to Jimmi\
 , Felipe’s devoted doctor\, who secretly performs as the drag artist Est
 rellita.\nForced together by Felipe’s final wishes\, Pepe and Jimmi emba
 rk on a journey across Cuba to carry out his last request. What begins as 
 a reluctant partnership soon becomes an emotional road trip filled with un
 expected discoveries\, difficult conversations\, and moments of profound u
 nderstanding.\nSet against the vibrant landscapes of Cuba\, Baracoa is a h
 eartfelt story about reconciliation\, chosen family\, and finding common g
 round in the most unlikely places. Through humour\, and unforgettable perf
 ormances\, the film celebrates the transformative power of empathy and hum
 an connection.\nDon’t miss this powerful cinematic journey that bridges 
 generations\, identities\, and borders while exploring what it truly means
  to come home.
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/baracoa-presented-by-the-icff-festival-a
 t-the-distillery-district-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Battle of the Sexes: American Psycho
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T204500
UID:blogto-236723@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/18/original_imagedc351aa5-823b-4490-a263-acac9e8d62
 b1.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Battle of the Sexes is a series featuring films directed by wo
 men about men and films directed by men about women. Through titles like A
 merican Psycho\, La Captive\, Marnie\, and Birth\, our speakers will inter
 rogate how films reinforce or distort gender roles. The series is hosted b
 y Gabrielle Marceau from In the Mood Magazine.\n“Based on the novel by B
 rett Easton Ellis\, Mary Harron’s American Psycho is a searing\, funny\,
  and stylish portrait of the men at the top of the financial food chain. T
 he film follows Patrick Bateman\, a Wall Street investment banker with fas
 tidious grooming\, a tastefully severe apartment\, and unstoppable murdero
 us impulses.\nWhile Harron’s sleek and campy thriller is taking on the y
 uppies of the 1980s\, her film remains painfully relevant in an era of per
 sonal optimization\, unchecked wealth hoarding\, and extreme misogyny fuel
 led by online discourse.”\nIntroduced by Quinn Henderson\, a writer with
  work in the
LOCATION:Fox Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/battle-of-the-sexes-american-psycho-toro
 nto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
