BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Curator Walkthrough: David Liss on Don't Look Back
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T150000
UID:blogto-236692@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/17/original_image498c0cdb-b459-46f5-abc7-e05b09d354
 2f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:What goes into choosing 17 artists with wide-ranging practices
  to tell 65 years of the story of Canada's largest and longest-running out
 door art fair? Join curator David Liss for a guided tour of Don't Look Bac
 k and find out. He'll walk you through the thinking\, the themes\, and the
  contemporary relevance — past TOAF artists alongside present ones\, all
  part of a story that continues to evolve.\nDavid Liss is an independent c
 urator\, writer and artist currently living in Toronto. From 2000 to 2020 
 he was Director\, Curator and Artistic Director of the Museum of Contempor
 ary Art Toronto. From 1995 to 2000 he was Director and Curator of the Gall
 ery of the Saidye Bronfman Centre for the Arts in Montreal. During the ear
 ly 1990s he contributed art and music reviews to the Montreal Gazette\, Vi
 ce\, Canadian Art\, and other publications. Since the late 1980s he has or
 ganized\, curated\, written texts and essays\, published books and develop
 ed interdisciplinary.
LOCATION:Koffler301
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/curator-walkthrough-david-liss-on-dont-l
 ook-back-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:daltonists and Juana Go-Go
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T220000
UID:blogto-236832@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/22/original_image1f9bf763-d4fe-421d-b157-0516f971b2
 58.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Small World Music\nJoin us for the official Small
  World Music Festival After Party at Lula Lounge\, where the celebration c
 ontinues with a final night of live music\, culture\, and global sounds.\n
 Experience performances that move from Latin rhythms to Polish contemporar
 y jazz with Afrobeat influences.\nThe daltonists take the stage with an im
 mersive set that pushes musical boundaries\, blending contemporary jazz im
 provisation with Afrobeats\, dub\, electronic textures\, and African club 
 rhythms.\nTo keep the dance floor energized\, Juana Go-Gó\, delivers all-
 vinyl DJ sets that move through Latin funk\, soul\, cumbia\, salsa\, and g
 lobal grooves.\nFor full festival programming details\, visit the Small Wo
 rld Music Festival page and explore the complete 3-day festival lineup.\nA
 bout the Artists:\ndaltonists\nA trio from Poland\, the daltonists is an e
 xperimentation band whose name draws from the concept of colour blindness.
  That idea has become their guiding idée fixe—a central inspiration and
  driving force behind their music. Their music combines the colours of con
 temporary jazz\, afrobeat\, dub\, and African club music.\nDespite their s
 hort existence (June 2021)\, daltonists have become a sensation on the loc
 al scene\, playing at several prestigious festivals in Poland\, including 
 Jazz Jantar\, True Tone Festival and OFF Festival. At the Crossroads Showc
 ase Festival in Ostrava\, they won a special award for the best band selec
 ted by music industry professionals\, which resulted in invitations to fur
 ther festivals in 2026/2027 (Sunfest Festival and Ottawa Jazz in Canada\, 
 Colours of Ostrava in the Czech Republic\, Jazz Fest in Brussels) and othe
 rs.\nTheir second album\, "Gradient" was released in November 2025 by the 
 British label Folded Music.\nJuana Go-Gó\nJuana Go-Gó is a Cali born\, T
 oronto-based DJ\, vinyl selector\, and cultural curator known for crafting
  immersive dance floor experiences rooted in Latin and global sounds. Her 
 sets move as travesías sonoras—sonic journeys that connect memory\, dia
 spora\, and movement\, blending genres with intention\, depth\, and a stro
 ng sense of storytelling.\nWith a deep commitment to musical discovery and
  preservation\, Juana Go-Gó’s selections draw from vinyl culture\, weav
 ing together Latin funk\, soul\, cumbia\, salsa\, and global rhythms into 
 dynamic\, genre-fluid sets. Her approach is both archival and forward-look
 ing\, creating spaces where tradition and contemporary expression meet on 
 the dance floor.\nDoors open at 7:00PM\nDinner reservations can be made at
  https://www.lula.ca/reservations\nFor accessibility requests and addition
 al inquiries\, please contact us at boxoffice@smallworldmusic.com\n—-\nF
 unded by the Government of Canada\, Canada Council for the Arts\, the Gove
 rnment of Ontario\, Ontario Arts Council\,  the Toronto Arts Council\, and
 \nthe City of Toronto—through the Community Celebration Support Fund.\nF
 inancé par le gouvernement du Canada\, Conseil des arts du Canada\, le go
 uvernement du Ontario\,  Conseil des arts du Ontario\, le Conseil des arts
  de Toronto\, et la Ville de Toronto.
LOCATION:Lula Lounge
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/daltonists-and-juana-go-go-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
