BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dog who stoically watched other pup chow down offered dream day at
  ballpark
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T150000
UID:blogto-236939@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/24/original_imagec85029cd-e936-4f84-b17a-ba95d0f59a
 4f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:MIAMI\, FL — Baseball fans and dog lovers alike are celebrat
 ing a heartwarming moment Visit Our Official here <a href="https://www.bon
 fire.com/miami-and-marlins-find-this-dog-dream-day-at/">miami and marlins 
 find this dog dream day at loandepot park shirt</a>\nafter the release of 
 the Miami And Marlins Find This Dog Dream Day At LoanDepot Park Shirt\, a 
 design inspired by a memorable day at LoanDepot Park. The shirt captures t
 he joy and excitement of a beloved canine enjoying a dream experience at t
 he home of the Miami Marlins\, creating a unique crossover between sports 
 culture and pet appreciation.\nThe story behind the shirt has quickly gain
 ed attention among fans who enjoy feel-good moments connected to their fav
 orite teams. Featuring a playful concept centered around a dog’s unforge
 ttable day at the ballpark\, the design reflects the welcoming atmosphere 
 that many fans associate with Marlins events. It also highlights the growi
 ng popularity of pet-themed apparel in the sports merchandise market.\nLoa
 nDepot Park has become known for hosting special fan experiences\, communi
 ty events\, and family-friendly activities throughout the baseball season.
  The idea of a dog enjoying a dream day at the stadium resonates with many
  supporters who consider their pets part of the family. As a result\, the 
 shirt has generated buzz on social media\, where fans have shared photos\,
  reactions\, and stories about attending games with fellow animal lovers.\
 nThe design combines baseball-inspired elements with lighthearted graphics
  that celebrate the connection between sports and pets. Supporters appreci
 ate the shirt not only as a piece of fan apparel but also as a reminder of
  the memorable experiences that sports venues can create beyond the game i
 tself.\nCollectors of unique Marlins-themed merchandise have also shown in
 terest in the release. Limited-event and novelty shirts often become popul
 ar keepsakes\, especially when they commemorate moments that capture the s
 pirit of a community. The “Dream Day” theme offers a positive and upli
 fting message that appeals to fans of all ages.\nAs excitement continues t
 o grow\, the Miami And Marlins Find This Dog Dream Day At LoanDepot Park S
 hirt stands out as a fun tribute to baseball\, companionship\, and unforge
 ttable memories. Whether worn at the stadium or around town\, the shirt ce
 lebrates a story that has brought smiles to both baseball enthusiasts and 
 dog lovers across the fan community.
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/dog-who-stoically-watched-other-pup-chow
 -down-offered-dream-day-at-ballpark-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EVERYTHING IS POLITICAL - SATIRE with CALE BAIN
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T150000
UID:blogto-236183@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/06/original_imagee549d767-0181-469a-8867-416fb5c063
 34.jpg
DESCRIPTION:It's part lecture\, part seminar\, part workshop.\nThe lecture
  part is an examination of satire\, a look at what it is\, what conditions
  are needed for it to exist\, what it can (or does not) achieve. It's part
  sociology\, part literature studies\, part comedy studies.\nThe seminar p
 uts pen to paper and gives people a chance to see how satire works by putt
 ing it into practice in groups using fairytale structures to challenge heg
 emonies\, looking at using familiar genres and tropes to interrogate patri
 archies and supremacies\, for testing power structures on the whole.\nFina
 lly\, after putting this stuff in on paper\, we get up and try to put it i
 nto place in scenes.\nSee\, the ultimate thesis is that every act is a pol
 itical one\, whether we're aware of the politics engaged in those acts or 
 not. I'm trying to get people to be aware and to try to say something clea
 r\, or be able to choose to say something clear if they're inclined to.\nC
 ale Bain was the founding Artistic Director of Improv Theatre Sydney and a
  journalism and comedy scholar from the University of Technology Sydney in
  Australia. He’s performed\, taught and directed improv all over the wor
 ld.\nBring a pencil and paper and a newspaper or magazine.\nCOST: $100 + T
 ax
LOCATION:Comedy Bar East
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/everything-is-political-satire-with-cale
 -bain-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Footy T.O.Gether: Canada vs South Africa Watch Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260628T170000
UID:blogto-237000@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/24/original_image4448141c-3475-4913-b4cc-96191b55c1
 c0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:FREE TO ATTEND! ⚽\nNobody saw this coming. Now Canada has to
  deal with it.\n🇨🇦 Canada vs 🇿🇦 South Africa — a Round of 32
  knockout clash nobody predicted at the start of the tournament. South Afr
 ica shocked South Korea in the final group game to earn their spot. Canada
  drew with Bosnia\, demolished Qatar 6-0\, and pushed Switzerland all the 
 way. Now it’s knockout football and one of these sides is going home Sun
 day afternoon.\nToronto26 is bringing Canada vs South Africa to Bloor Stre
 et as part of Footy T.O.Gether\, our watch party series running all summer
  long across three side-by-side venues.\nCrafty Coyote | 511 Bloor St W\nM
 ezcalero | 509 Bloor St W\nVictory Cafe | 440 Bloor St W\nExpect big match
  energy\, packed rooms\, good people\, and the kind of atmosphere Toronto 
 keeps proving it can deliver. ⚽🍻\nWe’ve packed out El Clásico and 
 the UCL Final and mobilized thousands of fans across the city. Come see wh
 y Toronto football keeps showing up.\nThree side-by-side venues. One great
  atmosphere. Get there early\, grab your spot\, and let the atmosphere bui
 ld.\nToronto football is here all summer. 🌟\nWho is Toronto26?\nWe run 
 Toronto’s top soccer watch parties\, building hype while helping grow th
 e city’s soccer culture. Through our high-energy events\, we bring fans 
 and communities together around the game.\nToronto26 is also part of the M
 atchday Social network\, a growing movement that connects supporters beyon
 d the stadium by creating spaces where football culture can thrive.\nBecau
 se the game isn’t only played on the pitch. It lives wherever fans gathe
 r.\nToronto is a soccer city.\nwww.toronto26.com | info@toronto26.com | in
 fo@matchdaysocial.com | #TorontoIsASoccerCity\n* Independent watch party. 
 Not affiliated with or endorsed by any governing football body\, any natio
 nal football federation\, or participating teams.
LOCATION:Crafty Coyote
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/footy-together-canada-vs-south-africa-wa
 tch-party-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
