BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Official Tubi Pride Merch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T130000
UID:blogto-237014@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/25/original_image083ddec7-f549-4478-bd97-f9f75a0eed
 68.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Official Tubi Pride Merch Generates Massive Buzz Online\nThe O
 fficial Tubi Pride Merch collection website https://www.bonfire.com/offici
 al-tubi-pride-merch/ has become one of the most talked-about Pride Month r
 eleases\, attracting attention across social media platforms and quickly s
 elling out popular items. Known for its playful online personality and fre
 e streaming service\, Tubi has successfully turned its Pride merchandise i
 nto a viral sensation.\nThe collection features a variety of colorful appa
 rel and accessories inspired by Tubi’s signature purple-and-yellow brand
 ing. Among the standout products are the “Proud Tubi Gay” tank top\, b
 randed baseball caps\, basketball shorts\, and other limited-edition piece
 s designed specifically for Pride celebrations. The merchandise combines h
 umor\, bold graphics\, and LGBTQ+ pride themes\, creating a collection tha
 t resonates with the platform’s audience.\nMuch of the excitement surrou
 nding the Official Tubi Pride Merch launch came after images of the collec
 tion spread across social media. Fans praised the designs for being fun\, 
 creative\, and different from the more traditional Pride products released
  by many major brands. The collection quickly gained viral attention\, wit
 h many shoppers reporting that items sold out within minutes of becoming a
 vailable online.\nThe merchandise was designed in collaboration with creat
 or Cole Poska\, who has previously worked on projects for Tubi. His distin
 ctive style helped create a collection that reflects the streaming service
 ’s lighthearted and internet-savvy brand identity.\nBeyond the merchandi
 se itself\, the collection highlights Tubi’s ongoing support for LGBTQ+ 
 audiences. The streaming platform is widely recognized for offering a larg
 e selection of queer films\, documentaries\, and independent productions\,
  making Pride-themed merchandise a natural extension of its content offeri
 ngs.\nAs Pride Month continues\, the success of Official Tubi Pride Merch 
 demonstrates how brands can connect with audiences through authenticity\, 
 humor\, and community engagement. With demand remaining high and many item
 s already sold out\, the collection has established itself as one of the s
 tandout Pride merchandise releases of the year\, further strengthening Tub
 i’s reputation among fans and LGBTQ+ viewers alike.
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/official-tubi-pride-merch-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Potato Potato Saves the World? at The Toronto Fringe Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T194500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T204500
UID:blogto-236408@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/11/original_image86b2b2bf-a767-4a11-845c-a00e45204c
 34.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Sketch Troupe Potato Potato (Audience Choice TO Sketchfest\, W
 inners Sketch to the Death) is proud to announce their new show Potato Pot
 ato Saves the World (?) at the Toronto Fringe Festival from June 30th- Jul
 y 11th at Soulpepper’s Kevin & Roger Garland Cabaret. Potato Potato Save
 s the World (?) blends musical theatre and sketch comedy to show the best 
 (and worst) of humanity in the face of an alien invasion.\nFresh off a red
 -hot run at Montreal and Toronto Sketchfests\, Potato Potato Saves the Wor
 ld(?) is Potato Potato’s most ambitious show yet: a blend of musical the
 atre and sketch comedy combining Potato Potato’s hit sketches with new o
 riginal music. It's a 60-minute narrative tour de force that finds humour 
 in climate change\, A.I.\, Canadian politics\, and the millennial/ Gen Z e
 xperience\, as the group endeavours to defend the Earth from alien invader
 s in an intergalactic court of law. But\, as they review some of their hit
  sketches about politics and the environment\, the group is faced with the
  question- is humanity worth saving after all?\nCreated with support from 
 the Sketch Comedy Project Fund\, Potato Potato Saves the World(?) takes fu
 ll advantage of the troupe’s degrees in Musical Theatre and Devising. It
 ’s part sketch revue\, part musical theatre\, and all Potato Potato\, in
  an examination of the fate of art in a world headed toward AI. This isn't
  just a sketch show\, it's a desperate bid to save humanity. Catch the act
 ion in Potato Potato Saves the World(?).
LOCATION:Soulpepper Theatre's Kevin & Roger Garland Cabaret
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/potato-potato-saves-the-world-at-the-tor
 onto-fringe-festival-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
