 visible women\, Mother Mary and Mary Magdalene\, through a feminist lens. 
 This intimate audience-immersive production explores grief\, voice\, power
 \, emotional visibility\, and historical erasure\, inviting audiences into
  a deeply human story that feels as relevant today as it does centuries la
 ter.\nRunning June 30 through July 11 at Cake Cabaret as part of the 2026 
 Toronto Fringe Festival\, Mary\, Mary intentionally collapses the distance
  between performer and audience\, creating an experience that begins and e
 nds within the audience itself.\nTickets are available via Toronto Fringe 
 Website.
