BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LADIES' DAY
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T231500
UID:blogto-236802@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/22/original_image89104a03-ab37-4a14-9b4c-9c0d1442e8
 b3.jpg
DESCRIPTION:LADIES' DAY is a brand new 75 minute play premiering at the To
 ronto Fringe Festival.\nFOUR-TIME 2026 DORA NOMINEES 1EAST PRODUCTIONS BRI
 NGS SUBURBAN DRAMEDY "LADIES' DAY" TO TORONTO FRINGE\nWindsor\, 1966. Ever
 y Thursday\, a group of suburban housewives trade their aprons for cold be
 ers\, cigarettes\, and dirty jokes at the neighbourhood’s first backyard
  pool. "Ladies’ Day" is a riotous\, booze-fueled escape from domesticity
 — but underneath the laughter and Labatt's\, our gals navigate alcoholis
 m\, hidden desires\, and the quiet suffocation of lives lived for everyone
  else.\nInspired by the playwright's grandmother's real-life Ladies' Days.
  A brand new play about what "the good old days" really looked like on the
  inside\, and what happens when women stop performing happiness long enoug
 h to find each other.\nFrom the creators of Romeo Pimp (four 2025/26 Dora 
 Mavor Moore nominations including Outstanding New Play)\, Cheap Wine (Audi
 ence Choice TOSketchfest 2025\, Sketchiest Sketch Troupe TOSketchfest 2023
 )\, and Pride & Prejudice (a new adaptation premiered by Wren Theatre).\np
 laywright: Jesse McQueen & Jack Creaghan\ndirector: Jack Creaghan\nmovemen
 t director: Shanda Bezic\nstage manager: Sarah Brawn\ndramaturg: Ferron De
 lcy\nfeaturing:\nShanda Bezic\nBlair MacMillan\nJennifer McEwen\nJesse McQ
 ueen\nCarson Pinch
LOCATION:VideoCabaret - Deanne Taylor Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/ladies-day-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
