BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Play in Toronto Fringe 2026\, He-r'tz\, by 78 Productions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T191500
UID:blogto-236786@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/20/original_imagef72d79f8-d4a3-4dc9-9b09-c0f8362e6a
 a8.jpg
DESCRIPTION:He-r’tz\, part of the Toronto Fringe 2026\, is an interdisci
 plinary physical theatre piece exploring the collective memory of a genera
 tion displaced and caught between worlds. Devoid of dialogue\, the perform
 ance communicates through movement\, sound\, and light—asserting that tr
 auma is not just translated\, but transmitted.\nIt is a story that lives i
 n the body\, resonating with the universal struggles of powerlessness\, gr
 ief\, and survival. It is a love letter to everyone who has ever had to st
 art over.
LOCATION:Video Cabaret - Deanne Taylor Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/new-play-in-toronto-fringe-2026-he-rtz-b
 y-78-productions-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
