 fb.jpg
DESCRIPTION:In this based-on-a-true-story comedy\, Miho dives into the imm
 igrant experience with wit\, fantasy\, and zero mercy. From awkward misund
 erstandings to unspoken biases\, she unpacks what it really means to speak
  English "differently." Equal parts hilarious and thought-provoking\, this
  show fires jokes while celebrating the beauty of every voice.\nPerformanc
 es (Runtime - 55 mins):\n2nd July\, 9:45pm\n4th July\, 7:15pm\n5th July\, 
 4:00pm\n8th July\, 9:15pm\n9th July\, 4:30pm\n10th July\, 7:15pm\n11th Jul
 y\, 9:30pm\n12th July\, 3:15pm\nTickets go on sale: June 3\nCheck out the 
 Toronto Fringe Festival Website (fringetoronto.com)\nInstagram: @theimprop
 eridentity
LOCATION:Native Earth's Minogitoon Workspace Giizis Studio
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-improper-identity-toronto/
