BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DANSE MACABRE by Rhoma Spencer - Toronto Fringe Festival 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T194500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260703T210000
UID:blogto-236491@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/12/original_image2c0228ef-3e57-46c9-96f3-82c618f277
 63.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Winner of the 2026 Toronto Fringe New Play Contest\, Danse Mac
 abre\, an electrifying Caribbean theatrical work by acclaimed playwright R
 homa Spencer\, arrives at a moment when Canadian stages are ready—if not
  overdue—for a story of this depth and urgency.\nRooted in the vibrant\,
  complex world of Carnival\, Danse Macabre goes beyond spectacle to explor
 e the powerful intersection of culture\, Queer identity\, and resistance. 
 It offers a bold\, unflinching examination of the history and politics of 
 anti-Black racism\, woven into the lived experience of ‘playing mas.’\
 nThis is theatre that speaks to both heart and history.\nRunning from July
  3rd - July 12th\, at Tarragon Theatre Mainspace\, it's not to be missed!
LOCATION:Tarragon Theatre Mainspace
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/danse-macabre-by-rhoma-spencer-toronto-f
 ringe-festival-2026-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
