 gto.com/events/2026/06/23/original_image4b5b0a66-ef46-4d8e-8c00-1927523e02
 ab.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Chicago/Detroit based ensemble Teiku reframes unique and rare 
 Eastern European ancestral passover melodies in an improvised music settin
 g. The expansive possibilities of instant composition\, the ritualistic or
 igins of the melodies\, and the inspiration of jazz pioneers like Ornette 
 Coleman and Muhal Richard Abrams all contribute to the immersive world of 
 Teiku.\nThe band features bass clarinetist Jason Stein (Natural Informatio
 n Society\, Hearts and Minds)\, bassist Jaribu Shahid (Art Ensemble of Chi
 cago\, Sun Ra Arkestra\, Geri Allen)\, and founders pianist Josh Harlow (V
 incent Davis\, Wadada Leo Smith) and percussionist Jonathan Barahal (saajt
 ak\, Wadada Leo Smith\, Michael Formanek). Teiku is releasing their sophom
 ore album\, Klang\, this June on Ginkgo Records\,\nDoors 6pm / Concert 7pm
 \n$40adv. $50door
LOCATION:CONTXT by Trane
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/teiku-klang-album-release-tour-feat-jaso
 n-stein-and-jaribu-shahid-toronto/
