BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Not Your Average Painting Workshop - Intuitive Abstract
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260705T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260705T130000
UID:blogto-236088@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/04/original_image21618ad3-acf2-43e4-9b9e-4aa693da8d
 f8.jpg
DESCRIPTION:bymonina is collaborating with Toronto's oldest curated flea m
 arket\, The Toronto Flea Market in Leslieville! In this workshop\, you'll 
 have a once-in-a-lifetime experience to explore intuition through the subt
 le act of painting. Unlike traditional painting workshops\, there will be 
 no image to copy from - the inspiration is you.\nIntuition is defined as t
 he ability to understand immediately without conscious reasoning. Painting
  requires small decisions at every turn - what colour colour should I use?
  What paintbrush do I like? How much pressure should I apply? The goal of 
 this workshop is to be able to answer low stakes questions without hesitat
 ion - trusting your body to lead you in the right direction.\nWhat to Expe
 ct\n- Light meditation to set your energy for the workshop\n- Lesson in ac
 rylic painting and intuitive abstract\n- Healing card to inspire your proc
 ess\n- 1-1 Guidance throughout the workshop\n- Access to blue & white acry
 lic paint\, primed canvas\, range of paintbrushes and palette knives\n- BY
 OB (Bring Your Own Blanket)\n- Mini Take-Home spiritual healing kit from @
 the.mindfulawakening\nWhether you’re a curious beginner or a creative so
 ul\, this workshop is an experience in connecting with your intuition thro
 ugh the act of painting. All materials provided (except BYOB Bring Your Ow
 n Blanket). This is a safe and welcoming space.\n​Rain or shine\, settle
  into an unforgettable experience under the canopy of Ashbridge Estate's w
 illow tree. Come with an open mind and a curious soul\, leave with a canva
 s that’s entirely your own.\nBe sure to follow @thetorontoflea for all m
 arket updates and @bymonina to watch the journey.\nSubscribe to Toronto Fl
 ea Market Newsletter here: https://torontoflea.com/home After the workshop
 \, check out the flea market - support local!\nWorkshop led by Monina Cepe
 da (bymonina)\, Filipino-Canadian intuitive abstract artist and small busi
 ness owner of bymonina ceramics. Alumni instructor at Art Works Art School
  and previous exhibitor at J.D. Carrier Art Gallery and Art Space Connect 
 Gallery. Monina approaches workshops with a playful and open nature. Get r
 eady to laugh!
LOCATION:Ashbridge Estate
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/not-your-average-painting-workshop-intui
 tive-abstract-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
