 94.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join the Toronto Holocaust Museum for summer Professional Deve
 lopment\, exclusively for grade 10 classroom educators.\nThis session will
  explore the changes to the Grade 10 History curriculum\, using our new re
 source\, Unpacking Canadian Antisemitism. This resource examines how antis
 emitism shaped Canada from the rise of Nazism (1929-1945) to its ongoing p
 resence in today’s schools\, communities\, and institutions. It will als
 o feature a workshop exploring how to navigate challenging topics in the c
 lassroom.\nCoffee and lunch are included (Kosher “Kashrut” observed). 
 Please ensure you sign up using an email address you will check during the
  summer\, so you receive important seminar communications\, including dire
 ctions and confirmations.\nNeeds-based scholarships are available. If you 
 would like to attend but cost is a barrier\, please email us at education@
 thethm.org and we will do our best to accommodate.\nNotice of Filming and 
 Photography\nPlease be advised that photographs may be taken during this p
 rofessional development session for marketing purposes. Feel free to reach
  out to education@thethm.org with any questions.
LOCATION:Toronto Holocaust Museum
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/grade-10-educator-professional-developme
 nt-summer-2026-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
