BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DesignTO Tours: Deacon Residence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260708T190000
UID:blogto-236111@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/05/original_imageba542689-95bb-43f0-9eee-6e7561b4a0
 98.jpg
DESCRIPTION:As part of our charitable fundraising efforts\, join DesignTO 
 for an exclusive house tour in Toronto’s Little Italy neighbourhood.\nTh
 e remaking of this Toronto home was a collaboration between owner Tom Deac
 on and his longtime friend Andrew Jones\, both graduates of architecture a
 t the University of Toronto. Soon after graduating\, Deacon shifted his fo
 cus to furniture design\, going on to a successful career designing a broa
 d range of seating mostly for large scale production. Jones\, after adding
  a degree in furniture design from the Royal College of Art in London\, al
 so developed a career in furniture and product design while continuing to 
 practice architecture and interior design. This dual experience forms the 
 foundation of his work.\nOne starting point for their approach was a desir
 e to make a home for Tom’s collection of furniture and art\, inherited\,
  collected\, and made by Tom himself\, manipulating light\, space\, and ma
 terials to create a rich yet quiet series of spaces that would enhance the
  experience of the eclectic collection rather than compete with it.\nThe 
 “bones” of the project was a 4-storey\, 1893 brick Victorian house on 
 an historic street in Toronto’s Little Italy neighbourhood. Previous own
 ers had stripped all historic details\, inside and out so while Tom decide
 d on a meticulous recreation of the original facade using English brick\, 
 the closest match now available to the original Toronto red brick\, the in
 terior presented a “tabula rasa” for the designers who approached the 
 design meticulously.\nExperience this special space yourself by joining th
 e tour led by homeowner Tom Deacon\, designer Andrew Jones\, and DesignTO 
 Artistic Director Deborah Wang.\nThe exact address for the house tour will
  be shared with ticket holders. Please respect the privacy of the homeowne
 rs by keeping their address confidential.
LOCATION:Deacon Residence
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/designto-tours-deacon-residence-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
