  a double-bill of Charpentier. For the chamber music lovers\, you can hear
  the Miró\, Poiesis\, and Balourdet Quartets\, as well as members of the 
 Dover\, Calidore\, Viano\, New Orford\, and Brentano String Quartets. Bel 
 canto superstars Erin Morley and Lawrence Brownlee present their celebrate
 d Golden Age program — one of the top 25 albums of 2025 by the New York 
 Times.\nGold Laureate of the 2025 Honens International Piano Competition 
 Élisabeth Pion makes her Toronto debut alongside harpist Emmanuel Ceysson
  with the TSM Festival Orchestra\, under the baton of Ryan Haskins. Other 
 performances include mezzo-soprano Sasha Cooke\, pianist Inon Barnatan\, v
 iolinist Timothy Chooi in recital with pianist Jon Kimura Parker\, with a 
 program dedicated to Jascha Heifetz\, Kleztory\, members of the Chamber Mu
 sic Society of Lincoln Center\, and more! Come get your classical music fi
 x for summer\, with 50+ events between July 9 - August 1!
LOCATION:Multiple Venues
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-summer-music-festival-toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vector Festival Who Cares For The Cyborg?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T210000
UID:blogto-236375@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/10/original_imagef4ea951e-5ffb-45ba-9ff2-81cf91e038
 e6.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Who Cares for the Cyborg?\, digs into the 𝘨𝘶𝘵𝘴\, 
 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘨𝘶𝘯𝘬\, 𝘢𝘯𝘥 𝘵𝘩𝘦 𝘨𝘦𝘢𝘳
 𝘴 of the mechanical bodies that make up our technologies.\n📀📀The 
 14th edition of Vector Festival will search for parallels between computer
  and human bodies\, looking at how we overheat and sweat\, bleed coolant\,
  and are circuited through our veins. In an era of thinner phones and hidd
 en wires\, the physical footprint of our technology is obscured\, erasing 
 the reminder for maintenance and care. How does this impact those with ins
 ulin pumps at their hips or prosthetic arms that require batteries? Can we
  push back against the techno-optomist desire to create posthuman bodies b
 y seeking to understand the machines already in our homes?\n🚨PROGRAM HI
 GHLIGHTS VF26🚨\n🌐Flagship Exhibiton | Who Cares for the Cyborg? | Ju
 ly 9 – 19\nCurated by Ciar O'Mahony\n💽Gamemaking Residency Showcase |
  Where Are Your Guts? | July 16 – 19\nCurated by Bracy Appeikumoh\n🦷A
 ugmented Reality Residency Multi-site Exhibition | July 9 – Aug 8\nCurat
 ed by Christina Dovolis & Evangeline Y Brooks\, presented with SariSari Xc
 hange and supported by the City of Toronto's Community Celebration Support
  Fund.\n🪫Special Event | Insomniac Film Fest: Now That's Acting! | July
  10\nPresented by Insomniac Film Festival\nRegistration\, more details\, a
 nd updates with workshops soon to be announced @ interaccess.org 👁️
 👁️
LOCATION:InterAccess
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/vector-festival-who-cares-for-the-cyborg
 -toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
