BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Latin Friday: Compota de Manana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260710T230000
UID:blogto-234719@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/05/06/original_imageead2af34-d1d3-47bc-bbbd-b805bbf4c7
 57.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A special international edition of our Latin Fridays showcasin
 g one of the leading groups on the international Latin music scene\, direc
 t from Barcelona!\nCanada’s premier Latin music and dance club invites y
 ou to experience an unforgettable night of salsa — dinner\, dancing\, an
 d live music all under one roof!\nBook a table for dinner and dancing\, or
  arrive after 9 PM to head straight to the dance floor.\nEvening Schedule\
 n� 7:00 PM – Doors open for dinner and drinks\n� 9:00 PM – Salsa l
 esson (no partner needed!)\n� 10:00 PM – Live salsa set\n� 11:00 PM 
 – Keep the energy going with Lula's Global Late Night Party!\nAbout the 
 Band\nBorn in Barcelona and deeply rooted in Cuban musical traditions\, Co
 mpota de Manana has built a reputation as one of the most original and exc
 iting acts on the contemporary Latin music scene. Their sound blends the i
 ntensity and sophistication of Cuban timba with modern influences\, creati
 ng high-energy performances that have filled clubs and festival stages acr
 oss Europe. Since the release of their acclaimed debut album La Alternatim
 ba\, the group has appeared at major festivals including Couleur Café and
  Toros y Salsa\, earning praise from international media and sold-out audi
 ences along the way.\nLed by bassist and composer Erik Castillo — known 
 internationally for his work with Nathy Peluso — the band returned with 
 the ambitious album Cuestión de Tiempo\, featuring collaborations with Cu
 ban icons including Mayito Rivera and Alexander Abreu. Their official show
 case at WOMEX 2025 confirmed the group’s growing international profile\,
  followed by a major performance alongside Los Van Van at the Festival Int
 ernacional Cubano in Orange. Compota de Manana arrives in Toronto fresh fr
 om performances across Europe and Latin America with a live show that is e
 xplosive\, dance-driven\, and impossible to stand still through.\nWhy Lula
  is unique:\nThe only venue of its kind in North America\, Lula Lounge fea
 tures a rotating roster of more than a dozen full salsa orchestras every F
 riday and Saturday—year-round. Our stage welcomes the best local talent 
 alongside special guests from across Canada and the Americas\, offering a 
 one-of-a-kind salsa experience in a warm\, colourful\, and inclusive space
LOCATION:Lula Lounge
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/latin-friday-compota-de-manana-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
