 gto.com/events/2026/05/19/original_image381ce499-38e6-4e12-a102-6be0385cdf
 dc.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This programme traces a journey through solitude\, song\, and 
 survival. Bach’s radiant E Major Partita opens with brilliance and poise
 . American voices emerge in Copland’s beloved folk settings — simple\,
  tender\, and deeply human. Kelly-Marie Murphy’s Give Me Phoenix Wings T
 o Fly rises from devastation toward renewal\, and Shostakovich’s Piano Q
 uintet closes the evening with brooding intensity\, razor-sharp wit\, and 
 ultimately\, hard-won light — music of clarity\, courage\, and rebirth.
LOCATION:Walter Hall
