BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:There'll Likely Be Michael Jackson Vigils Throughout the Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T210000
UID:blogto-236617@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/06/16/original_image86fd8b78-1126-4ebb-92d8-dc2a09d793
 03.jpg
DESCRIPTION:International Premiere\nThe shocking news of Michael Jackson
 ’s death is witnessed through thousands of found footage video reactions
  in director Marcus Batto’s collage-tornado of a film. Remixing early Yo
 uTube vlogs\, news coverage\, song fragments and more\, There’ll Likely 
 Be Michael Jackson Vigils Throughout the Night is both a potent exercise i
 n modern internet archiving and a time capsule for a bygone era of the wor
 ld wide web. More honest than any traditional MJ biopic could ever aspire 
 to be\, Batto’s film defines Jackson through a web of the world’s wide
 -ranging POV’s in this one very specific moment in time: eschewing valou
 rization while exploring the idea of celebrity deification. And it’s fun
 ny too! Get your graphic tees and your shutter shades on… we’re going 
 back to 2009!\nThis international premiere will be followed by a Q&A with 
 director Marcus Batto.\nThe feature will be preceded by the Toronto premie
 re of the short film Take a Look Around (D: Colby Richardson): an experime
 ntal doc about a video artist who brings a power drill camera contraption 
 to the CNE.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/therell-likely-be-michael-jackson-vigils
 -throughout-the-night-toronto/
