 4f.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Spend a morning with the Nature Centre experiencing the joys a
 nd challenges of summer birding! While birds are harder to spot through th
 e leaves\, summer residents like the charismatic swifts and swallows are a
  joy to watch over Grenadier Pond and savannah. This is a casual birding w
 alk where all skill levels are welcome.\nThis is a beginner-friendly hike.
  The Nature Centre will have binoculars to borrow for the event.\nPrice: P
 ay What You Can ($0\, $5\, $8\, $10)\nAges: 16+ years\nMeeting Location: H
 igh Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodge Drive
