BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Panamerican Food Festival 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T235900
UID:blogto-236394@blogto.com
DESCRIPTION:ArtsXplosion Cultural Society is thrilled to announce that the
  14th annual Panamerican Food & Music Festival (PANAMFEST) will take place
  July 24–26\, 2026 at Nathan Phillips Square\, with a VIP Gala Opening R
 eception on July 16 at Daniels Spectrum. The FREE 3-day festival is expect
 ed to welcome over 90\,000 visitors and will feature groundbreaking new pr
 ogramming aligned with Toronto as a FIFA World Cup 2026 Host City.\n“PAN
 AMFEST has grown from a small waterfront gathering to one of Toronto’s m
 ost beloved and economically significant cultural events\,” said Daniel 
 Garcia Herreros\, Executive Director of ArtsXplosion Cultural Society\, wh
 ich produces the festival. “In 2026\, we’re proud to welcome the world
  to Toronto at a historic moment—combining the passion of Panamerican cu
 lture with the global excitement of the FIFA World Cup.”\nCelebrating th
 e Dominican Republic as Feature Country\nThe 2026 festival will spotlight 
 the Dominican Republic as the Feature Country\, presenting an immersive sh
 owcase of Dominican music\, dance\, cuisine\, and visual arts. Audiences w
 ill experience authentic performances by artists from the island alongside
  Toronto’s vibrant Dominican Canadian community. “The Dominican Republ
 ic has a profound cultural legacy\, from merengue and bachata to world-ren
 owned gastronomy\,” said Garcia Herreros. “We are honoured to share th
 eir creativity and spirit with Toronto and visitors from around the world.
 ”\nNew: World Cup of Traditional Food Competition\nFor the first time in
  PANAMFEST’s history\, the festival will present the World Cup of Tradit
 ional Food—a multi-round culinary competition where chefs from across th
 e Americas compete head-to-head in live cooking challenges. Audiences will
  taste signature dishes and vote in real time\, celebrating the incredible
  diversity of Panamerican cuisine from ceviche to jerk chicken.\n“Food i
 s culture\, and this competition brings together the flavours that unite u
 s across borders\,” said Mary Luz Mejia\, PANAMFEST’s Culinary Curator
 . “It’s a chance for Torontonians and visitors to experience authentic
  tastes from 25 countries—all in one incredible weekend.”\nWhat to Exp
 ect at PANAMFEST 2026\nOver three days\, PANAMFEST will present:\n\n45+ li
 ve musical & folkloric performances representing 25 countries across the A
 mericas\nThe International Panamerican Parade featuring 500+ costumed perf
 ormers\nSalsa Dance Competition\, Dominican Merengue Party\, and Next Pana
 merican Star youth talent showcase\nWorld Cup of Street Eats Competition: 
 6 chefs compete to be the “best” in class with their country’s top s
 treet food as chosen by the public\nCulinary demonstrations by 20+ chefs s
 howcasing traditional and contemporary Panamerican cooking\nCoffee Tasting
 \nCaribbean show – Carnival Spice\nActivation Zone with soccer-themed cu
 ltural programming\, developed in partnership with York United FC\nPanamer
 ican Market with food vendors\, food truck\, artisans\, and entrepreneurs 
 from across the Americas\nIndigenous land acknowledgement and dedicated In
 digenous performance programming\nChildren’s cultural workshops in dance
 \, percussion\, and visual arts\n\nThe festival is entirely FREE and open 
 to the public.
LOCATION:Nathan Phillips Square
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/panamerican-food-festival-2026/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Project Grizzly - 30th Anniversary
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T190000
