 19.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Genius often reveals itself early — and boldly. Dohnányi’
 s Piano Quintet\, written at 17 and praised by Brahms\, brims with youthfu
 l ambition. Mendelssohn’s C minor Trio shows that same prodigious spirit
  transformed into sweeping Romantic authority. Prokofiev’s brilliant Son
 ata for Two Violins opens the night with sharp wit and kinetic drive. An e
 vening of fearless invention and blazing artistry.
