 f3.jpg
DESCRIPTION:In this beginner-friendly workshop learn how to identify commo
 n birds in High Park. Focusing on some of the park’s most frequently spo
 tted species\, you’ll learn to recognize key field marks and characteris
 tics that can help you identify birds. We’ll also explore how to use eBi
 rd to track your sightings\, find birding hotspots\, and contribute to com
 munity science. The workshop combines classroom-style instruction with a g
 uided walk through the park\, giving you the chance to practice your new s
 kills and observe birds in their natural habitat.\nPrice: $35\nAges: 18+ y
 ears\nMeeting Location: High Park Forest School\, 375 Colborne Lodge Drive
