BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Toronto Poetry Festival  2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260912T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T050000
UID:blogto-226346@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2025/11/02/original_image62edfac6-1423-4324-a644-29c2db22a5
 e2.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Poetry Festival Sets Date for 2026 Celebration\nThe To
 ronto Poetry Festival has officially set its date for Saturday\, September
  12\, 2026. The event will be held from 11:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.\, offering
  a full day of literary engagement.\nThe festival will once again convene 
 in the open air at Taylor Creek Park (Spot#5\, 260 Dawes Road\, East York\
 , ON M4C 5C4)\, providing a serene\, natural amphitheater for the spoken w
 ord.\nLaunched in 2024\, the festival has successfully established itself 
 as an annual tradition\, having completed two well-received iterations. It
  fosters a celebratory atmosphere by featuring a diverse ensemble of poets
 \, including both English-language Canadian wordsmiths and multilingual ar
 tists presenting original work in their native tongues.\nBuilding on this 
 success\, the 2026 program is slated for expansion. It will introduce new 
 conceptual elements to complement its core offerings of original poetry re
 adings and recitations\, signalling a dynamic evolution of the event. The 
 festival remains committed to accessibility\, offering free admission to t
 he public with no tickets required.\nAs a multilingual and multinational g
 athering\, the Toronto Poetry Festival vividly illustrates Canada's cultur
 al mosaic. Embodying Canadian values with a global sensibility\, the event
  is cementing its place as an annual autumn tradition\, set against the ba
 ckdrop of the season's vibrant foliage. It is steadily garnering significa
 nt interest and popularity within the literary community.
LOCATION:Taylor Creek Park
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-poetry-festival-2026-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
