 f Media\, Creative Arts\, and Design.\nHow to Survive a Bear Attack\, by C
 laire Cameron\, finalist for the 2025 Governor General’s Literary Award 
 in Non-Fiction\, investigates a rare bear attack in Algonquin Park while r
 eflecting on her own battle with genetic cancer. Blending nature writing\,
  true crime and memoir\, Cameron explores fear\, resilience and survival.\
 nBy the Lake Book Club hosts six Tuesday-night events from February to Dec
 ember with top Canadian authors and Humber Polytechnics alumni. Each in-pe
